=== Euclidean inball and transference constants ===
[1/14,13/14]^13 = (1/2)1 + (3/7)[-1,1]^13.
For x in n^perp with ||x||_2<=1, every |x_i|<=1 and projection(x)=x;
hence the projected zonotope contains the closed ball B(c,3/7).
A counterexample has dist(c,Lambda)>3/7, so mu(Lambda)>3/7.
Using 2 mu(Lambda) lambda_1(Lambda*)<=12 gives lambda_1(Lambda*)<14.
More exactly, the projected cube's centred Euclidean inradius factor is
  rho(n)=min_(i<j) (n_i+n_j)/sqrt(n_i^2+n_j^2)
        =(n_min+n_max)/sqrt(n_min^2+n_max^2).
Thus lambda_1<14 sqrt(n_min^2+n_max^2)/(n_min+n_max); the universal
bound is its unbounded-spread limit.

=== Exact integer coefficient consequences ===
Every transference relation a satisfies sum a_i^2<=195 and |a_i|<=13.
The exact integer optimization gives ||a||_1<=50.
The unique sorted absolute arithmetic extremizer is (3,3,4,...,4),
with squared norm 194 and l1 norm 50 (realizability is not asserted).
Bounded-spread integer caps (R=n_max/n_min):
  R : square-norm cap, l1 cap
  2: 108, 37
  3: 122, 39
  5: 141, 42
  13: 169, 46
  21: 178, 47
  50: 188, 49

