=== Labelled Euclidean-ball universe ===
All nonzero labelled integer vectors with sum a_i^2<=195: 711202814025242.
Primitive vectors: 711119925281794; primitive support>=2 modulo sign: 355559962640884.
This is more than 2782564628359 times smaller than THM-3743's l1<=356 ambient universe.

=== Rank-eleven Hadamard join ===
If the short row lies outside THM-2052's rank-11 span, Hadamard gives
  max(n_i) <= 11639011567946276516330452125265832396450210671398535269626998205847761612881723251682730932524351641613494572161619231675129410858204
(134 digits). If it lies inside, that span contains a row with squared norm<=195.
Support at most three is automatically inside because coefficient height<=13<91^6.

=== Half-lattice parity sidecar and safe hostile ===
The inball center c=(1/2)projection(1) satisfies 2c in Lambda.
Because a counterexample has c notin Lambda=Lambda**, some (not necessarily short)
dual relation has <a,c>=1/2 mod 1, equivalently sum a_i is odd.
Banaszczyk transference alone does not force the norm-<14 row to be this odd row.
The safe AP (1,...,13) has relation (1,-2,1), squared norm 6, and
a valid boundary loneliness time t=1/14. Short resonance remains necessary,
never sufficient; owner, phase, sign partition, and arrival are still lost.

=== Scope verdict ===
CITED + PROVED-ALGEBRA target: counterexample => a nonzero Graver relation
with ||a||_2<14, sum a_i^2<=195, ||a||_1<=50, and |a_i|<=13.
The citation supplies only Euclidean transference; all printed finite constants are exact.
This does not prove LRC(14).
